spec field_reduce

description:
  Modular reduction of an arbitrary-width integer residue into the canonical range
  `[0, p)` of a prime field `GF(p)`. This is the final step of Montgomery
  multiplication (and of `from_bytes`): given a value `x` in `[0, 2p)`, produce
  `x` if `x < p` else `x - p`, without branching on the comparison result.

inputs:
   x : [u64; LIMBS]   // an integer in [0, 2p), little-endian limbs

outputs:
   result : [u64; LIMBS]

assumes:
   0 <= x < 2p

ensures:
   // functional correctness: result is x reduced modulo p, canonical.
   result == x mod p
   0 <= result < p
   // constant-time contract: the comparison `x >= p` and the conditional
   // subtraction must not leak through the execution trace.
   execution_trace ⟂ x

non_leaks:
   - the `x >= p` comparison is performed limb-wise with a borrow/mask, not a
     secret-dependent branch
   - the subtraction `x - p` is applied via a constant-time select (cmov), so
     both `x` and `x - p` are computed unconditionally and one is chosen by mask

verification:
   // discharged by the `tests/smoke.rs` round-trip (from_bytes(to_bytes(x)) == x)
   // and by Wycheproof non-canonical encoding rejection in
   // `tests/kat/field_reduce.json` (see `tests/kat/PROVENANCE.md`).
